    "description": "At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter\u2014giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.\n\nAbout the Engineering team\n\nThe Engineering team builds systems that power Affirm\u2019s mission. We take pride in our craft, building reliable, performant, and scalable solutions that touch every part of the business. Whether we\u2019re enabling new ways to pay, ensuring our platforms can scale to the most demanding levels in the industry, or developing seamless servicing experiences, our focus is on solving complex problems through exceptional engineering.\n\nAbout the role\n\nAffirm\u2019s Identity team is mission-critical to the customer checkout experience. When a customer chooses Affirm, one of the first steps is an identity check, and our ability to make the right decision directly impacts conversion, revenue, fraud exposure, and regulatory compliance.\n\nOur team owns Identity for all markets outside North America, playing a key role in Affirm\u2019s international expansion. We are responsible for KYC, user lifecycle management, and identity decisioning across multiple regulatory environments. As an Engineering Manager on our team, you\u2019ll help shape how Affirm adapts its core Identity platform to new market dynamics, customer expectations, and compliance requirements.\n\nWhat you\u2019ll do\n\nYou will lead and grow a well-balanced team of engineers \u2013 setting clear expectations, giving direct feedback, and developing each engineer toward their next level.\n\nYou will own the team\u2019s technical strategy and multi-quarter roadmap, tying it to major experience initiatives that build customer trust and move Affirm\u2019s business, including large-scale redesigns and structural improvements to the identity verification journey.\n\nYou will empower your tech lead and engineers to hold the design and quality bar, supporting them hands-on throughout technical design and cross-functional alignment.\n\nYou will own the availability, reliability, and performance of consumer-critical systems \u2013 on-call, incident response, and reducing operational toil.\n\nYou will drive alignment across multiple organizations and influence roadmaps on partner experience and foundational teams.\n\nYou will partner across Product, Design, and Analytics, and other Engineering teams, building trust and taking part in cross-functional efforts.\n\nWhat we look f",
