    "description": "About the team\n\nThe Control Plane Platform team is building the shared foundation that every product in ClickHouse Cloud is built and shipped on. We give ClickHouse engineering teams one place to own and deploy their product, remove the overhead of rebuilding common plumbing, and keep the customer experience consistent as the number of integrating teams grows. The team owns API gateways and API standards, shared platform services, deployment and infrastructure patterns, testing and CI, local developer experience and Control Plane observability.\n\nAbout the role\n\nWe\u2019re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead our Platform team. This is a high-impact, high-trust role at the center of our Cloud product, combining people leadership, technical direction, product thinking, and operational ownership while maintaining the reliability customers expect.\n\nYou\u2019ll work hand-in-hand with Product, Infrastructure, Security, Support, and engineering teams across ClickHouse.\n\nThis role goes beyond engineering leadership. Together with your team, you\u2019ll help shape how new products and teams will integrate and deploy their applications in ClickHouse Cloud.\n\nWhat You\u2019ll Do\n\n- Lead, coach, and grow a high-performing team - recruit to a high bar, set crisp expectations, give direct feedback and career development, and manage performance \u2014 while fostering a healthy, inclusive environment built on empathy, psychological safety, trust, and a high technical bar.\n\n- Own outcomes across the platform surface: API gateways and API standards, shared platform services (event bus, notifications, feature flags, websockets, audit records), deployment and infrastructure patterns, CI and testing, local developer experience, disaster recovery, and Control Plane observability.\n\n- Treat the integrating teams as your customers and measure success by their delivery velocity and adoption of the platform, not only by what your team ships.\n\n- Guide architecture and help senior engineers make explicit, sound tradeoffs. land cross-cutting migrations, deprecations, and contract changes across teams without stalling product delivery.\n\n- Jump into designs and code for complex areas - gateway routing and auth/RBAC enforcement, spec-driven code generation, event delivery semantics and idempotency, multi-region rollout safety.\n\n- Build the culture of operational excellence: Own SLOs, reliability, on-call quali",
