    "description": "ABOUT THE MANAGED POSTGRES TEAM\n\nThe Managed Postgres team is building a high-performance, reliable PostgreSQL service within ClickHouse Cloud. We give developers a familiar PostgreSQL experience, remove operational burden, and connect transactional Postgres workloads with real-time analytics in ClickHouse. The team owns provisioning, high availability, backup and recovery, upgrades, observability, performance, security, and developer experience.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead the team building and operating ClickHouse Managed Postgres. You will combine people leadership, technical direction, product thinking, and operational ownership while maintaining the reliability customers expect.\n\nYou will report directly to Kaushik Iska, who leads the Managed Postgres organization. You will partner closely with Product, Design, Infrastructure, Security, Support, and engineering teams across ClickHouse.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n- Lead, coach, and grow a high-performing team through clear expectations, feedback, development, and direct performance management.\n\n- Own outcomes across provisioning, fleet management, failover, point-in-time recovery, upgrades, observability, performance, and security.\n\n- Turn customer and business needs into a multi-quarter roadmap with incremental milestones.\n\n- Guide architecture and help senior engineers make explicit, sound tradeoffs.\n\n- Raise operational quality across SLOs, on-call, incidents, maintenance, and automation.\n\n- Work directly with customers and turn recurring pain into product improvements.\n\n- Align dependencies, surface risks early, and keep execution predictable across a distributed organization.\n\n- Hire the right mix of PostgreSQL, systems, infrastructure, reliability, and product engineering talent while fostering ownership and clear technical debate.\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n- 8+ years in software engineering, including 3+ years managing engineers in infrastructure, databases, or developer platforms.\n\n- Experience building and operating a customer-facing stateful service with demanding availability, durability, security, and performance requirements.\n\n- Working knowledge of PostgreSQL or managed relational databases, including replication, WAL, high availability, recovery, upgrades, observability, or performance diagnosis.\n\n- Technical credibility to engage deeply in architecture and incidents ",
