    "description": "The Autonomous Ops & Maintenance (ATOM)Team\u00a0 is developing an innovative platform that leverages artificial intelligence and automated systems to empower engineering groups in safely executing complex operations and software maintenance. Their primary objective is to minimize repetitive toil while delivering the precise visibility, oversight, and trust necessary to run automated solutions in mission-critical environments.\n\nConsider it an intelligent virtual collaborator operating alongside development and infrastructure engineers, directly offloading routine operational overhead that currently requires manual intervention.\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to help us design and scale our foundational architecture. In this role, you will synthesize vast technical datasets into rich structured knowledge, engineer AI-driven components capable of analyzing intricate operational workflows, and construct highly reliable systems to execute automated modifications seamlessly.\n\nAt Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.\n\nWhat You\u2019ll Do:\n\nLead a greenfield initiative from inception to scale, shaping foundational product architecture, engaging directly with users to refine early concepts\n\nBuild mission-critical solutions that customers depend on daily\n\nBuild fault-tolerant, horizontally scalable solutions running in multi-tenant environments\n\nWho You Are:\n\nYou have 6+ years of experience\n\nYou have a BS/MS/PhD in a scientific field or equivalent experience\n\nYou are proficient in Go\n\nYou are comfortable building and operating production services end to end: You will independently own features and components, work through ambiguous technical problems, and be responsible for the reliability, observability, and operational quality of what you ship\n\nYou have experience with large scale distributed systems\n\nYou have demonstrated ability to use AI coding tools in day-to-day workflows and validate, critique, and refine AI-generated output\n\nBonus Point: You have experience with Kubernetes, workflow orchestration systems, or building AI agents\n\nDatadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one.",
