    "directApplyUrl": "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/granola/ed52eb55-cb81-4ed8-b97b-92b477876f9e/application",
    "description": "Hey! We're team Granola \ud83d\udc4b\n\nIf you haven't already, you should check out what we're building https://www.granola.ai/, and why you should work here https://www.granola.ai/jobs.\n\nWe are looking for a self-starting engineer, passionate about applying the latest advancements in LLMs to create user-centric products.\n\nThe Core Harness team builds the systems that turn models into useful, reliable agents at Granola: the agent loop, tools, memory, context management and execution environment. We own how those pieces work together, so agents can understand a user\u2019s work, take action across their tools and follow through on complex tasks.\n\nAs an AI Engineer on the team, you\u2019ll work across model behaviour and the systems that shape it. That might mean deciding what an agent should remember, helping it recover when a tool fails, or redesigning its execution loop to make use of a new model\u2019s capabilities.\n\nWHY YOU MIGHT BE A GOOD FIT\n\n- You\u2019ve built with models and investigated their failures. You can explain where a system struggled, how you diagnosed the problem and what made it better.\n\n- You think across the whole agent. You\u2019re interested in how model behaviour, context, memory, tools and execution interact, and can reason about which part needs to change.\n\n- You have judgment about agent/model behaviour. You notice when an agent is being unhelpful, taking unnecessary steps or acting with too little information. You care about making it feel capable, responsive and trustworthy.\n\n- You enjoy a field where the answers keep changing. You try new capabilities, develop your own understanding of their strengths and limitations, and revisit earlier decisions when the evidence changes.\n\n- Love working in a startup environment (you either have experience working in a startup or are really drawn to the zero-to-one phase)\n\n- Are fascinated by LLMs. You love to play with them, figure out what makes them tick and get them to do what you want. You scour the web and reddit for others doing the same (you probably follow @goodside on twitter)\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n- Own the development and application of LLM-based features end-to-end\n\n- Build and maintain evaluation frameworks for prompt iteration and semantic retrieval\n\n- Optimize embeddings and vector stores for performance and scalability\n\n- Interact with users to understand their problems and design solutions\n\n- Stay up-to-dat",
