    "description": "About the job\n\nTurn complex engineering changes into controlled, traceable actions that keep advanced AI hardware moving forward.\n\nAs an Engineering Change Analyst, you\u2019ll coordinate product and manufacturing changes across complex hardware. You\u2019ll bring structure and momentum to every change.\n\nYou\u2019ll help ensure changes are complete, reviewed and implemented correctly. Your work will improve visibility and maintain accurate product records.\n\nYou\u2019ll coordinate ECRs, ECOs and Deviations throughout their lifecycle. You\u2019ll also support impact assessments, change reviews and clear communication across teams.\n\nThis role puts you at the centre of engineering, manufacturing, quality and supply chain. You\u2019ll see how decisions become controlled product changes.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nYou\u2019ll join Configuration Management within Manufacturing Operations. The team owns product configuration, engineering change control, product data governance and PLM processes.\n\nDay to day, you\u2019ll work across technical teams and manufacturing partners. You\u2019ll track actions, surface blockers and keep changes progressing.\n\nGood decisions depend on accurate information and clear ownership. You\u2019ll help teams understand impacts, document decisions and resolve issues before changes move forward.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for\n\nEssential\n\nExperience in engineering change control, product lifecycle management, or manufacturing operations.\n\nExperience using PLM, ERP, or engineering data management systems, with a solid understanding of bills of materials (BOMs), part numbering, revision control, and engineering documentation.\n\nStrong organisational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to coordinate multiple changes, track actions to completion, and escalate issues appropriately.\n\nStrong written and verbal communication skills, with the confidence to collaborate across Engineering, Manufacturing, Quality, and Supply Chain teams.\n\nDesirable\n\nExperience in electronics, semiconductors, computing, or complex hardware product development, including contract manufacturing or global production environments.\n\nPractical experience with controlled change processes, such as Engineering Change Requests (ECRs), Engineering Change Orders (ECOs), Engineering Change Notices (ECNs), or deviations.\n\nExperience using Arena PLM and supporting or coordinating Change Review Boards or Change Control Boards.\n\nA rel",
