    "description": "About the job\n\nHelp shape the first moments of life for the next generation of AI processors.\n\nYou'll lead the bring-up and characterisation of Graphcore's silicon devices and system platforms. Your work will ensure products perform reliably before they reach customers.\n\nYou'll build and lead a team that develops characterisation plans, automates testing, and analyses results across silicon and system platforms. You'll work closely with architecture, silicon, hardware, operations and product teams to solve complex technical challenges.\n\nThis is a hands-on technical leadership role with the opportunity to influence product design, shape new capabilities, and build a team from the ground up.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nYou'll join a newly formed team within Manufacturing Operations and help define how bring-up and characterisation is delivered at Graphcore. Your decisions will shape the team's direction as it grows.\n\nThe team works closely with colleagues across Bristol, Cambridge and Taiwan. Success comes from solving problems together, sharing data, and making informed engineering decisions.\n\nYou'll be trusted to take ownership, remove blockers, and improve how work is done. We value people who speak up, challenge assumptions, and turn ideas into practical solutions.\n\nWhat we're looking for\n\nEssential\n\nProven track record of delivering technical outcomes as an individual contributor, manager, or project manager, with strong communication and stakeholder management skills.\n\nSolid experience in silicon digital device design, bring-up, and characterisation, with a good understanding of silicon process technology and its impact on transistor- and system-level performance.\n\nStrong knowledge of high-performance processors, system-on-chip (SoC) architectures, and high-speed digital interfaces such as PCIe, Ethernet, and DDR.\n\nExperience with measurement automation, data analysis, and developing code or scripts to support automated testing and analysis workflows.\n\nBachelor's degree (or equivalent practical experience), with a background understanding of ATE systems and their role in silicon characterisation.\n\nDesirable\n\nKnowledge of PCBA and system level technologies.\n\nProject management experience.\n\nBenefits\n\nUnlimited annual leave\n\nUp to 5% matched pension\n\nPhantom equity \u2013 share in Graphcore's success\n\nTrue flexibility in how and where you work\n\nOffice spaces designed",
