    "description": "About the job\n\nDesign the high-speed signal paths that let advanced AI compute systems perform at datacentre scale.\n\nAs a Signal Integrity Engineer, you will shape the electrical performance of Graphcore hardware platforms. Your work will help 112Gbps and 224Gbps SERDES, DDR and processor interfaces operate within demanding system budgets.\n\nYou will develop, extract and simulate PCB structures across production systems and test boards. You will define launches, via structures, transmission lines, stack-ups and low-loss materials for future designs.\n\nThis role spans simulation, lab validation and practical design influence. You will work from concept through prototype bring-up, debug, validation and support for manufacture.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nYou will join the Hardware Engineering team, working closely with PCB, package substrate, system architecture and supplier teams. Work moves through simulation, design review, lab evidence and practical trade-offs.\n\nYou will be expected to own signal integrity decisions across complex board and package interfaces. The team values careful analysis, pace and clear communication when problems need action.\n\nDecisions are made close to the engineering detail. You will challenge designs, guide constraints and help teams reach the best performance possible.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for\n\n\u00b7 Strong experience in high-speed digital circuit development, with deep signal and power integrity knowledge\n\n\u00b7 Experience with high-frequency SERDES design and validation, including tens of GHz operation\n\n\u00b7 Expertise using tools such as ANSYS SIWave, HFSS, Mentor HyperLynx or similar\n\n\u00b7 Ability to design BGA and connector launches, via structures and transmission lines for GHz signals\n\n\u00b7 Hands-on lab experience using VNAs, high-speed oscilloscopes and signal generators\n\n\u00b7 Rigorous approach to design, debug and validation, with strong ownership and communication skills\n\nWhile we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.\n\nBenefits\n\n\u00b7 Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility\n\n\u00b7 Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work\n\n\u00b7 Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension\n\n\u00b7 Phant",
