    "description": "1891\n\nSignal Integrity Measurement Engineer\n\nLocation: Austin\n\nAbout the Role\n\nValidate signal integrity (SI) and power integrity (PI) for advanced compute platforms, focusing on hands-on measurement, electrical compliance, troubleshooting, and simulation correlation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nDevelop measurement plans and design of experiments (DOE) for board-to-board, cable, backplane, blade-, and rack-level interconnects.\n\nMeasure scattering parameters (S-parameters), insertion loss, return loss, impedance, crosstalk, eye diagrams, jitter, timing margins, and bit error rates.\n\nDesign printed circuit board (PCB) test fixtures; perform calibration, de-embedding, and electrical compliance testing against interface specifications and customer requirements.\n\nCorrelate measurements with simulations and troubleshoot issues with silicon, package, board, and system teams, interconnect vendors, and original design manufacturers (ODMs).\n\nPrepare validation and compliance reports covering methods, pass/fail results, performance margins, findings, and recommendations.\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\nHands-on expertise with vector network analyzers (VNAs), including performance network analyzers (PNAs); time-domain reflectometers (TDRs); bit error rate testers (BERTs); and high-speed oscilloscopes.\n\nStrong SI/PI fundamentals and experience with fixture characterization, repeatable measurements, DOE, and electrical compliance testing.\n\nStrong written and verbal communication skills for technical reporting and cross-functional collaboration.\n\nBachelor's or master's degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related field.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\nData center or hyperscale hardware experience; Python or MATLAB for measurement automation and analysis; familiarity with simulation tools and thermal or mechanical effects on SI/PI.\n\nTools / Technologies\n\nPeripheral Component Interconnect Express (PCIe) generations 4/5/6, Ethernet, Double Data Rate (DDR) memory, serializer/deserializer (SerDes) links, Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI), and Inter-Integrated Circuit (I\u00b2C).\n\nWhy Join Us\n\nWork with experienced technical leaders and interconnect partners to improve high-performance compute hardware.\n\nUSA Benefits\n\nIn addition to a competitive salary, Graphcore offers flexible working and a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your health, wellbeing and finan",
