    "description": "Salary Range: PLN 196,000 - 265,000\n\nSubject to alignment to the responsibilities\u00a0and duties of the role\n\nAbout the job\n\nAs a Software Engineer in the Collectives Team, you\u2019ll help develop the Collectives Communication Library for new AI hardware accelerators.\n\nThe library enables users to utilise large computing clusters, making communication an important part of running workloads at scale.\n\nYou\u2019ll implement, test and document library features, working with other teams to design and test new functionality.\n\nYou\u2019ll also troubleshoot complex technical issues and help integrate new hardware with the existing AI ecosystem.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nWe value face-to-face interaction and make time to meet in the office frequently. The team works in two-week sprints, with three stand-ups each week, fortnightly sprint planning and a weekly team meeting.\n\nWork is planned with input from the Technical Product Manager, covering both longer-term priorities and upcoming sprints. Engineers typically work in small groups on larger tasks or components, coordinating the work among themselves.\n\nThe team has a high level of technical expertise, with opportunities to attend thematic conferences and team outings roughly once a quarter.\n\nWhat we're looking for\n\nExperience developing software in C++, with experience using Python and C\n\nGood problem-solving skills and the ability to debug and resolve complex technical issues\n\nExperience with unit testing frameworks such as Boost.Test and Google Test\n\nExperience with build tools including CMake, Make and Ninja\n\nStrong understanding of version control systems, preferably Git\n\nKnowledge of multithreading, parallel computing and inter-process communication for efficient concurrent applications\n\nWhile we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.\n\nDesirable experience\n\nRDMA networking libraries such as libibverbs or libfabric\n\nParallel algorithms and optimisation for AI/ML and HPC systems\n\nContinuous Integration/Continuous Delivery pipelines, including GitHub Actions or GitLab CI\n\nCommunication libraries such as NCCL or MPI\n\nMachine learning frameworks such as PyTorch\n\nModern C++ standards, including C++17 and C++20\n\nBenefits\n\nFlexible working: ",
