    "description": "Staff Power Electronics Engineer\n\nAbout Us\n\nGraphcore\u00a0is a globally recognized leader in Artificial Intelligence computing systems. The company designs advanced semiconductors and data center hardware that provide the specialized processing power needed to drive AI innovation, while delivering the efficiency required to support its broader adoption.\n\nAs part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world\u2019s most transformative technologies.\n\nJob Overview:\n\nGraphcore is seeking a Senior Engineer, Power Engineering to aid in design, test, and development of the power delivery components from grid to chip. You will work closely with multiple cross-functional teams, including hardware engineers, firmware developers, and data center operations, to ensure the infrastructure we build meets customer requirements as well as attaining standards of performance, reliability, and scalability.\n\nThis role will be hybrid-remote, based in Milpitas, CA and will involve a significant in-laboratory component along with some work-from-home.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nContribute to the design and specification of the components and systems in the grid-to-chip power chain.\n\nBuild out the test environment and perform engineering test and validation of the grid-to-chip chain.\n\nDesign test hardware including the overall test environment, test fixtures, loads, and other devices to simulate various loading conditions and to evaluate the performance of the power chain.\u00a0 Testing includes basic function testing, robustness and reliability testing, high-power cycle testing, high-bandwidth power testing, energy storage testing, and numerous other types of tests involved in AI power system validation.\n\nDesign and prototype custom components as may be needed to support the Graphcore power architecture.\u00a0 This includes the low-level design of power conversion hardware and rapid prototyping.\n\nSupport the transition of system designs from test and validation into the manufacturing and production environments\n\nEnsure robustness of IT power in the presence of grid disturbances and make sure that IT power loads are compatible with grid power requirements (\u201cgood grid power citizen\u201d)\n\nProvide guidance to the power equipment manufacturers, ODM and engineering teams on the required testing and validation procedures for power hardware and firmware c",
