    "description": "About the job\n\nShape the power-delivery architecture behind Graphcore\u2019s high-performance AI compute systems, from voltage regulation through package, PCB and silicon.\n\nAs Staff Power Integrity Engineer, you will provide technical leadership on Graphcore\u2019s most complex power-delivery challenges. Your analysis and judgement will directly influence architecture and product decisions.\n\nYou will define modelling strategies, optimise decoupling and analyse PDN impedance, voltage droop, transient response and regulator interactions. You will turn complex results into clear engineering decisions, requirements and sign-off approaches.\n\nYou will lead significant PI issues through resolution and create alignment across silicon, package, board, power, systems and validation teams. You will also develop reusable methods and mentor engineers, raising power-integrity capability across Graphcore.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nThe Signal and Power Integrity team sits at the centre of Graphcore\u2019s hardware development. We work across disciplines to understand electrical behaviour and guide consequential architecture decisions.\n\nYou will own complex PI problems and drive them through to resolution. Decisions are grounded in modelling, first-principles reasoning, hardware evidence and clear assessment of uncertainty.\n\nYou will challenge assumptions, communicate risk clearly and help teams make pragmatic trade-offs. Technical influence matters more than reporting lines.\n\nWhat we\u2019re looking for\n\nDeep practical expertise in power integrity and complex power-delivery network design.\n\nStrong understanding of PDN impedance, transient behaviour, voltage droop, resonance, stability and decoupling across high-current digital systems.\n\nAbility to reason across silicon, package, PCB, voltage regulation and system boundaries.\n\nStrong capability in electromagnetic modelling, circuit simulation, model extraction and selecting appropriate abstraction methods.\n\nEngineering judgement to assess model validity, uncertainty and sensitivity, then translate analysis into architecture and product decisions.\n\nAbility to lead ambiguous technical work, influence across engineering disciplines, improve methodology and develop other engineers.\n\nWhile we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career br",
