    "description": "Salary Range: PLN 350,000 - 474,000 PLN\n\nSubject to alignment to the responsibilities\u00a0and duties of the role\n\nAbout the job\n\nAs a Staff Software Engineer in the Collectives Team, you\u2019ll drive the design and development of the Collectives Communication Library.\n\nThe library provides communication primitives optimised for high bandwidth and low latency at very high scale.\n\nYou\u2019ll lead development of the library for new AI hardware accelerators, working across design, implementation, testing and documentation.\n\nYou\u2019ll collaborate with other teams to develop new features, troubleshoot complex technical issues and integrate new hardware with the existing AI ecosystem.\n\nYou\u2019ll also mentor engineers and help drive technical excellence across the team.\n\nThe team and culture\n\nWe value face-to-face interaction and make time to meet in the office frequently. The team works in two-week sprints, with three stand-ups each week, fortnightly sprint planning and a weekly team meeting.\n\nWork is planned with input from the Technical Product Manager, covering both longer-term priorities and upcoming sprints. Engineers typically work in small groups on larger tasks or components, coordinating the work among themselves.\n\nThe team has a high level of technical expertise, with opportunities to attend thematic conferences and team outings roughly once a quarter.\n\nWhat we're looking for\n\nExtensive experience developing software in C++, with experience using Python and C\n\nStrong problem-solving skills and the ability to debug and resolve complex technical issues\n\nStrong understanding of multithreading and inter-process communication for efficient concurrent applications\n\nExperience with unit testing frameworks such as Boost.Test and Google Test\n\nProficiency with build tools including CMake, Make and Ninja, plus strong understanding of Git or similar version control systems\n\nStrong communication skills and experience working effectively with multinational teams and customers\n\nWhile we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.\n\nDesirable experience\n\nRDMA networking libraries such as libibverbs or libfabric\n\nParallel algorithms and optimisation for AI/ML and HPC systems\n\nContinuous Integration",
