    "description": "Who we are\n\nHelsing is a defence AI company. Our mission is to protect our democracies. We aim to achieve technological leadership, so that open societies can continue to make sovereign decisions and control their ethical standards.\n\nAs democracies, we believe we have a special responsibility to be thoughtful about the development and deployment of powerful technologies like AI. We take this responsibility seriously.\n\nWe are an ambitious and committed team of engineers, AI specialists and customer-facing programme managers. \u00a0We are looking for mission-driven people to join our European teams \u2013 and apply their skills to solve the most complex and impactful problems. We embrace an open and transparent culture that welcomes healthy debates on the use of technology in defence, its benefits, and its ethical implications.\n\nThe role\n\nWe\u00a0can't\u00a0flight-test our way to every answer,\u00a0the\u00a0range\u00a0time, the cost, and the sheer number of edge cases we need to cover make that impossible. Simulation is how we de-risk fast, explore the trade space before we cut metal, and understand what happens in scenarios\u00a0we'd\u00a0never dare fly for real. But we\u00a0don't\u00a0trust a model\u00a0that's\u00a0never been checked against\u00a0reality,\u00a0the sim exists to earn its way onto the range, not replace it.\n\nAs a Simulation Engineer on the Physical Products team, you'll build and maintain the modelling and simulation environments that let us understand how our platforms will actually behave,\u00a0aerodynamically, structurally, and as part of a full engagement,\u00a0before they're built, and\u00a0help interpret what happens after they fly.\u00a0You'll\u00a0work closely with GNC, mechanical, and systems engineers, and\u00a0you'll\u00a0be expected to hold your models to the same standard we hold our\u00a0hardware:\u00a0are they good enough to trust a decision on, and how do you\u00a0know.\n\nThe day-to-day\n\nBuild and\u00a0maintain\u00a0high-fidelity simulation environments,\u00a06-DOF vehicle dynamics, aerodynamics, structural, and/or engagement-level models,\u00a0depending on where your depth sits\n\nDevelop Monte Carlo and sensitivity analysis capability to explore performance across the real range of conditions a platform will see, not just the nominal case\n\nWork with GNC, mechanical, and systems engineers to define what needs modelling, at what fidelity, and why,\u00a0simulation effort should always trace back to a real design or operational question\n\nValidate models against real test and flig",
