    "description": "About the Team\n\nThe Intelligence and Investigations (I2) team provides intelligence to decision makers across OpenAI and investigates severe misuse of our products. I2\u2019s work saves lives: we disrupt real-world violence, protect children, and prevent catastrophic harms from AI misuse. We also draw on our investigations and in-depth analysis of a wide range of data sources to provide actionable quantitative and qualitative intelligence to OpenAI\u2019s leadership.\n\nI2 Engineering works hand in hand with I2\u2019s analysts and investigators, building tools that expand what human experts can understand and accomplish. Our tools help them make sense of vast and complex datasets, discover and measure on-platform and off-platform risk, and investigate severe misuse with greater speed, depth, and consistency.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe are looking for an Intelligence Systems Analyst who wants to work alongside investigators to understand difficult cases, contribute to analysis, and build tools and workflows that help the team do more. As investigators pursue leads, assess risks, and determine what happened, you\u2019ll see where better tools could help and build them.\n\nThe role combines hands-on software and data work with meaningful participation in investigations. Depending on the problem, you might trace activity across internal systems, write a query or small application, prototype an AI-assisted workflow, improve how evidence is assembled, or turn an investigator\u2019s recurring need into a durable product capability.\n\nYou will work closely with engineers, analysts, investigators, and other subject matter experts. Success requires enough operational understanding to contribute meaningfully to an investigation and enough technical ownership to build solutions that remain useful after the immediate case is resolved.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\n- Work directly alongside investigators on complex cases, helping develop leads, analyze evidence, and identify useful technical approaches.\n\n- Build and maintain software, data workflows, and internal tools that accelerate investigations of potential high-severity misuse or harm.\n\n- Use Python, SQL, and internal data systems to gather, connect, and analyze information relevant to investigative work.\n\n- Apply OpenAI\u2019s models to research, search, triage, synthesis, and evidence review in workflows that keep expert investigators informed and in control.",
