    "description": "About the Team\n\nThe Human Flourishing team\u2019s mission is to ensure AI systems understand and advance human flourishing. As AI becomes more capable and plays a larger role in people\u2019s lives, we want its human benefits to grow with its capabilities. The Human Flourishing team is part of the broader Personal AGI organization.\n\nOur approach has two parts. Firstly, we measure and improve models\u2019 understanding, capability, and propensity to act according to people\u2019s values and to help them achieve their long-term goals. Secondly, we directly scale tangible impact for users in human domains like education and mental health, working across research, product, and partnerships to increase the benefits over a billion people experience weekly when they use ChatGPT.\n\nOur recent work includes Beneficial RL https://alignment.openai.com/beneficial-rl/, which investigates how training for beneficial behavior generalizes across settings, and MentalHealthBench https://openai.com/index/introducing-mentalhealthbench/, a benchmark developed with mental health experts to evaluate realistic conversations.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe\u2019re looking for an exceptional, hands-on researcher to turn difficult-to-define signals of long-term flourishing into measurable improvements in model behavior. You\u2019ll help set research direction, build what is needed to test your ideas, and drive successful work into the models and products we ship.\n\nWe\u2019re especially interested in researchers with deep experience improving frontier models through pretraining or reinforcement learning (RL) / post-training, especially on less verifiable problems, or researchers who combine strong LLM skills with deep expertise in domains like education or mental health. Prior experience in these domains is not required.\n\nIn this role, you will\n\n- Develop scalable training methods across the training stack that improve how models understand people\u2019s values, support their agency, and help them achieve long-term goals.\n\n- Lead high-leverage research from an open question to a shipped improvement: choose a hard-to-define problem, iteratively define success, run experiments, and integrate into frontier models.\n\n- Build RL environments for difficult-to-verify outcomes, and study whether beneficial behavior generalizes across settings.\n\n- Create evaluations grounded in human expertise and feedback that reveal capability gaps, unintended ",
