    "description": "ABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Enterprise Trust & Governance team builds the control plane that lets the world\u2019s largest organizations deploy Perplexity broadly and with confidence. Computer and our agents work across a growing share of our customers\u2019 environments, tools, and models. For administrators, that makes precise, enforceable control essential: who can do what, with which data, through which agents, and within what usage limits. This team makes those controls easy to manage, reliable and consistent across every product, and transparent to the people accountable for them.\n\nThis is a product and platform engineering role with end-to-end ownership, from shaping the architecture and policy models to shipping the experiences our customers\u2019 administrators and security teams use every day. You\u2019ll work across product and infrastructure teams to turn complex enterprise requirements into reusable primitives and intuitive controls. The scope spans identity and provisioning, fine-grained role-based access across connectors, tool actions, and models, customer-managed encryption keys, admin APIs, audit logs, and policy and usage controls. Strong governance helps enterprises move from pilots to company-wide rollouts and gives them the confidence to entrust agents with greater responsibility over time.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n- Own enterprise identity and provisioning, including SSO (SAML/OIDC), SCIM, WorkOS integrations, and support for identity providers such as Okta and Microsoft Entra ID.\n\n- Build the permissions platform, with fine-grained roles and permissions for connectors, tool actions, models, and model effort levels, enforced consistently across products and agent workflows.\n\n- Design and ship secure, well-documented admin APIs for audit logs, members, groups, roles, and settings.\n\n- Build policy controls for model and feature availability, staged rollouts, model deprecations, usage and spend limits, alerts, and cost-center allocation.\n\n- Build admin-facing analytics for adoption, usage, spend, and policy enforcement, helping organizations measure value and manage their deployments.\n\n- Deliver audit logs and change notifications that help administrators investigate activity, track configuration changes, and support compliance.\n\n- Set the technical bar for authorization correctness and reliability, with fast, consistent, explainable permission checks, well-defined fa",
