    "description": "ABOUT SUPABASE\n\nSupabase is the Postgres development platform, built by developers for developers. We provide a complete backend solution including Database, Auth, Storage, Edge Functions, Realtime, and Vector Search. All services are deeply integrated and designed for growth. More than 9 million developers and 250,000+ customers now build on Supabase, and the majority of new databases on the platform are created by AI app builders \u2014 so the systems underneath have to stay reliable while they grow fast.\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nContainer Engineering (ConEng) owns the internal container platform that runs Supabase's multi-tenant, multi-region services \u2014 the managed Kubernetes platform that other engineering teams build and deploy on top of. We own cluster lifecycle and cluster classes, multi-cluster and multi-region topology, capacity, scheduling, isolation and runtime safety, the higher-level platform APIs, the Kubernetes deployment contract and Argo semantics, rollout primitives, and runtime configuration and secret injection.\n\nYour job is to make the platform itself trustworthy, observable, and cheap to operate at scale \u2014 and to raise the reliability bar for everyone who depends on it. This is not a gatekeeper role. You'll make the reliable path the easy path: building the automation and platform APIs that let product teams run safely by default, instrumenting what we operate, and making sure that when something breaks we detect it and recover fast.\n\nThe work spans three strength areas:\n\nTooling & ecosystem \u2014 deep knowledge of the container and orchestration landscape (Kubernetes, containerd/OCI, the CNCF ecosystem) and a clear point of view on how to compose it.\n\nSoftware engineering \u2014 designing and building the platform's automation, controllers, and internal tooling as production code, including solutions that don't come pre-shaped by an existing tool.\n\nOperational / SRE practice \u2014 the discipline (SLOs, error budgets, incident response, ORRs) that runs the platform at scale as a predictable one.\n\nWe expect you to be genuinely deep in at least one of these, and many of our strongest candidates are deep in two (usually leaning toward one). Bringing real strength across all three is rare and exceptional \u2014 and even then, no one is equally strong in all three at once, so you'd focus where you're most needed at any given time. Different profiles are welcome here; tell",
