    "description": "About Vercel:\n\nVercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what's next. For more than a decade we've helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.\n\nNow we're scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.\n\nAbout the role\n\nWe\u2019re looking for a Software Engineer to join our Platform team. You will build the observability systems that give Vercel visibility into how we build, ship, and operate our systems. Core Platform owns Vercel\u2019s reliability, resilience, and engineering velocity. We\u2019re looking for engineers to create observability for everything from cost attribution to deployment velocity, alongside the logs, metrics, and traces necessary to optimize how Vercel builds its systems. This is a role with a wide breadth where we quickly develop critical systems and improve the entire Vercel code base. You will report to Eric Larson, Engineering Manager, Platform and will be located onsite, hybrid, or remote.\n\nIf you\u2019re based within a pre-determined commuting distance of one of our offices (SF, NY, London, or Berlin), the role includes in-office anchor days on Monday, Tuesday, and Friday, even if the role is listed as remote. For location-specific details, please connect with our recruiting team.\n\nWhat you'll do\n\nDesign and build high-scale, internal observability systems (metrics, logs, and traces) that give engineering and the business visibility into Vercel's own infrastructure.\n\nBuild cost attribution and chargeback tooling so spend can be accurately mapped to the parts of the business driving it, reducing reliance on third-party tools like Datadog.\n\nPartner with Backend and Platform teams to instrument services for compliance, auditing, and record-keeping requirements.\n\nEvaluate, integrate, and help operate observability infrastructure across our existing vendors and the CNCF ecosystem.\n\nShip pragmatic, high-leverage visibility quickly that drives improvement in how we build, deploy, and operate our systems.\n\nWork closely with Backend and Platform engineers to scale observability infrastructure to the throughput and cardinality of Vercel's full production traffic.\n\nWhat you need\n\nProficient in TypeScript, with backend/infrastructure exper",
