    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About The Role\n\nWayve is building the next generation of embodied AI for autonomous driving. As we move from developing our core technology to deploying it across multiple vehicle platforms, OEM programmes and Robotaxi applications, the complexity of our software systems is growing significantly.\n\nWe\u2019re looking for a Distinguished Software Architect to help define how our software architecture evolves through this next phase of scale.\n\nThis is a highly cross-functional individual contributor role operating at the intersection of AI, robotics and large-scale software systems. You\u2019ll work across our onboard software, AI, simulation, training and inference, product engineering and Robotaxi teams, helping ensure that the systems we build today can scale across the products, hardware platforms and physical environments we need tomorrow.\n\nYou\u2019ll work alongside some of Wayve\u2019s most senior technical and engineering leaders on architectural decisions that cut across the entire technology stack, from AI models and compute through to the software running on physical vehicles.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\nYou\u2019ll operate across engineering organisations rather than within a single team, developing a deep understanding of how our AI, software and physical systems fit together and where architectural decisions in one area impact another.\n\nYou\u2019ll work closely with senior engineers and engineering leaders to identify architectural challenges, shape technical direction and lead major changes that span multiple teams.\n\nYou\u2019ll act as a trusted technical partner on some of our hardest engineering decisions, helping teams navigate trade-offs between immediate delivery needs and the long-term health and scalability of the overall system.\n\nA significant part of the role will be leading through technical credibility and influence, creating alignment across teams and helping raise the bar for software design and engineering practices across Wayve.\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on\n\n- Defining architectural direction across Wayve\u2019s software ecosystem as we scale our AI Driver",
