    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Engineering Teams\n\nThe Triage team in Application Software Japan, part of Product & Delivery, plays a critical role in the safety, reliability and triage efficiency of Wayve\u2019s ADAS+ systems. It bridges Detective Engineering, Triage Engineering and the component teams, so that root causes in real-world vehicle behaviour are found quickly and accurately and issues get resolved faster.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\nAs a Customer Integration Engineer (ML Triaging Engineer), you\u2019ll carry out first-level analysis of real-world run data and on-road interventions, work out likely root causes, and produce Top Issue reports across our test environments and operational domains. You\u2019ll work closely with Detective Engineers on ambiguous or complex runs and with Triage Engineers on automated triage solutions, and you\u2019ll own issues from identification through to documentation and reporting. As Wayve scales, so does the triage team, and you\u2019ll handle multiple triage tasks, requests and safety incidents at the same time.\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on:\n\n- Performing first-level analysis on real-world run data and on-road interventions.\n\n- Investigating issues to identify or narrow down likely root causes, and working with Detective Engineers on deeper analysis of ambiguous or complex runs.\n\n- Partnering with Triage Engineers to support and improve automated triage solutions.\n\n- Managing the full issue lifecycle: identification, investigation, resolution, documentation, reporting and follow-through.\n\n- Adding accurate metadata to interventions, including root cause labels, Jira links and comments.\n\n- Validating triage automation bots, offline metrics and simulation suites, and making sure outputs meet quality standards.\n\n- Giving feedback on triage tooling and suggesting improvements to usability and speed.\n\n- Taking part in regular standups to address emerging concerns, set priorities and adapt to process changes.\n\n- Contributing to a high standard of safety, quality and operational discipline across triage.\n\n\ud83d\ude4c You should apply if:\n\nEssential\n\n- Previous",
