    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Engineering Teams\n\nThe Application SW team sits within Application Engineering in Product & Delivery. We bridge AI innovation and production vehicles, defining and executing the strategy for integrating Wayve\u2019s autonomy stack into multiple OEM platforms, and working directly with automotive customers, including major Japanese OEMs.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\nAs an Application SW Engineer, you\u2019ll be responsible for the bring-up and early validation of our AI software stack on customer hardware platforms, ensuring it performs reliably across diverse SoCs and operating systems. You\u2019ll work closely with Verification, Release and OEM partner teams to make integration smooth and delivery dependable. Your time will be split across platform bring-up and integration, customer and partner engagement, and technical leadership, including helping to build the team.\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on:\n\n- Executing software bring-up on customer hardware platforms (e.g. NVIDIA Drive, Qualcomm Ride).\n\n- Porting and configuring Linux-based systems, QNX and Adaptive AUTOSAR environments.\n\n- Integrating and validating drivers, middleware and boot-time configurations.\n\n- Working with Verification and Release teams to integrate hardware into CI/CD, HIL and test infrastructure.\n\n- Working with OEM and Tier 1 teams to resolve hardware-specific integration issues.\n\n- Implementing system-level diagnostics, logging and secure boot configuration.\n\n- Developing automation for setup, flashing, health checks and test execution on target hardware.\n\n- Defining and executing the strategy for integrating our autonomy stack into multiple OEM platforms.\n\n- Building the team and providing technical leadership across integration work.\n\n\ud83d\ude4c You should apply if:\n\nEssential\n\n- 8+ years of experience in embedded or automotive software development, ideally with hands-on platform bring-up experience.\n\n- Strong proficiency in C/C++, Bash, and Python. Deep understanding of Linux-based embedded systems (Yocto, systemd, bootloaders, device trees).\n\n- Familiarity with QNX and Adaptive AUTO",
