    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Datasets Team\n\nWayve\u2019s Datasets team own the driving data that our AI Driver learns from, covering ingestion, annotation (automatic and manual), retrieval and data quality. Our data is growing from hundreds of petabytes towards exabyte scale, and not all of it is equally valuable for training. This team decides what we keep and where, and builds the systems that make those decisions work in practice.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\n- Implement and iterate filtering, retention and offload policies across hot, cold, archive and delete storage\n\n- Build the data movement and pipelines that our pre-ingestion selection model depends on\n\n- Decide where and how selection models run, balancing compute cost against data value\n\n- Build early, low-compute decision points that avoid expensive standardisation and enrichment of low-value data\n\n- Work with the storage and data infra teams, and monitor data quality to make sure our datasets reflect what model training needs\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on:\n\n- Turning our dataset strategy into working systems: moving, filtering, retaining and offloading driving data at hundreds of petabytes\n\n- The engineering behind our pre-ingestion selection mode(s)l: how data moves, where the model runs and how offload policies work\n\n- Delivering large, measurable storage-cost savings through early, low-compute decisions\n\n- Making sure our datasets contain the most useful behavioural and environmental coverage for training. This is as much a data quality challenge as a software engineering one\n\n- Working as a pair with our dataset strategy lead (who design and builds the models) and closely with the data infra team, shipping practical solutions quickly\n\n\ud83d\udc64 You should apply if:\n\n- You\u2019re a senior data or software engineer who has run data ingestion or data quality pipelines at petabyte scale\n\n- You\u2019re strong in Python and Spark, with cloud data engineering experience\n\n- You have good judgement on data filtering and quality, and know how to check you haven\u2019t discarded valuable data\n\n- You ship practical solutions quickly and",
