    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Driving Product Teams\n\nThe Driving Product team builds the AI driver's core behaviours, taking models from data and training through evaluation and on-road validation, then shipping them into the car on timelines measured in months, not years. The team's work has direct impact on high-priority commercial deliveries, including Nissan production and Robotaxi, and spans the full spectrum from Level 2 to Level 4 driving. It's a small, high-ownership team at a point of rapid growth, blending ML research with shipping-focused engineering.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\n- Develop the AI driver model architecture and training algorithms to introduce and enhance driving behaviours for L2/L3/L4\n\n- Own key parts of the training model lifecycle, including evaluation strategy, success metrics, and iteration planning\n\n- Mine, bucket, and curate real-world and synthetic data to teach specific driving behaviours, and implement data schemes to support training\n\n- Run and analyse on-road and offline experiments, translate results into clear next steps, and drive improvements through repeated training cycles\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you'll be working on:\n\n- Models that predict vehicle trajectories and interact directly with controllers and actuators, closing the loop between prediction and real-world vehicle performance\n\n- End-to-end work across data, model training, evaluation, deployment, and performance monitoring\n\n- On-road and off-road metrics that diagnose issues and drive data-led model iterations\n\n- Production-ready ML systems built with strong software engineering, quality, and reliability practices\n\n- Methods spanning reinforcement learning, behavioural cloning, and distillation, working with multi-sensor inputs such as camera, radar, and lidar where relevant\n\n\ud83d\udc64 You should apply if:\n\n- Proven track record training deep learning models with clear end-to-end ownership: data, training, evaluation, and iteration\n\n- You've taken ML models into production, working through real-world constraints, quality, and safety requirements\n\n- Strong Python skills and hands-on exp",
