    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Engineering Teams\n\nWayve\u2019s Robot Software team builds the onboard software used by our development fleet to enable autonomous driving and collect the data needed to train new driving models. The OS team curates Wayve\u2019s bespoke Linux and QNX distributions and works closely with hardware, supply chain, field engineering, reliability, and other Robot Software teams.\n\nYou\u2019ll help deliver a reliable, stable, and flexible operating-system platform that lets model developers and scientists iterate quickly while supporting new vehicles, sensors, peripherals, and product features.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\n- Build and maintain embedded Linux and QNX platform software, kernels, and device drivers.\n\n- Work with product, program, hardware, and engineering stakeholders to choose and deliver the right solutions.\n\n- Develop high-quality C and C++ software that is observable and debuggable on remotely operated vehicles.\n\n- Diagnose performance problems involving stack traces, core dumps, disk I/O, CPU load, memory, devices, and threading.\n\n- Improve fault tolerance, diagnostics, testing, documentation, tooling, and ease of use.\n\n- Mentor teammates and contribute to a strong engineering culture.\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on\n\n- Wayve\u2019s embedded Linux distribution, including Yocto, kernel configuration, device trees, boot sequence, and secure boot.\n\n- Linux kernel and device-driver support for new sensors, peripherals, and compute platforms.\n\n- High-throughput IPC middleware for robotics applications.\n\n- Robust diagnostics and remote debugging for vehicles with limited connectivity.\n\n- Stable platform software that supports rapid on-road experimentation and fleet operation.\n\n- Integration across NVIDIA Jetson, NVIDIA DRIVE, QNX, and future vehicle-compute platforms.\n\n\ud83d\ude4c You should apply if\n\n- You have strong C and C++ experience building high-performance embedded Linux system software.\n\n- You understand the full development lifecycle, from design through delivery and optimisation.\n\n- You have hands-on knowledge of embedded Linux kernels, device trees,",
