    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our datasets Team\n\nWayve's datasets team own the driving data that our AI Driver learns from, covering ingestion, annotation, retrieval and data quality. As our data grows from hundreds of petabytes towards exabyte scale, deciding what we keep, and where, is one of the biggest levers on both model quality and cost. This role sits at the centre of that challenge, shaping the data that model engineers train on across the company.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\n- Build and own the ingestion-time model that scores incoming driving data and routes it to hot, cold, archive or delete\n\n- Work with training teams to define the right data distributions for every model we're building\n\n- Deliver early storage-cost savings through practical heuristics, then develop ML-driven filtering\n\n- Partner with ingestion, annotation, retrieval, data quality, model training, AV/robotics, evaluation and storage teams to set company-wide data policy\n\n- Lead and work hands-on with a small group of software and ML engineers to build data provisioning and data provenance features into Corpus\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on\n\n- Defining our dataset content strategy: which data and metadata we need, and why, so training teams can select the most valuable data as smoothly as possible\n\n- Steering data selection by what our model engineers need right now. For example, if we're weak at unprotected right turns at traffic lights, those scenarios go straight to hot storage\n\n- Delivering large, measurable storage-cost savings as ingestion scales across our internal fleet and partner and OEM data\n\n- Evolving from practical heuristics to ML-driven filtering, and influencing what gets filtered at the vehicle and edge\n\n- Working as a pair with our Corpus Implementation Engineer to turn strategy into production systems\n\n\ud83d\ude4c You should apply if\n\n- You have strong autonomous-vehicle or robotics experience, working with large-scale driving, sensor or comparable data\n\n- You're a principal, hands-on ML engineer who has built models that score, select or filter data\n\n- You've operated at petabyte",
