    "description": "Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.\n\nWe build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.\n\nHere\u2019s what this particular role covers.\n\n\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f About our Driving Product Team\n\nThe Driving team owns Wayve's core end-to-end driving model, which directly shapes how our vehicles behave on the road. We take the backbone models and build the driving heads on top, and ship them into vehicles. That makes us the team closest to production. Our work is central to Wayve's Robotaxi launches around the world, so it ties directly to our near-term commercial milestones. We iterate fast: we find the top issues we see on the road, find their root causes, and fix them through data, model and evaluation changes. We work closely with other teams to solve issues that span the model and the vehicle.\n\n\ud83e\udde0 Your day-to-day\n\n- Lead a small team (up to five people) iterating on Robotaxi driving performance, balancing hands-on technical work with people leadership\n\n- Diagnose the highest-impact issues seen on the road, find their root causes and resolve them through data and model iteration\n\n- Own changes to data recipes, model architecture, evaluation and release readiness for the driving model\n\n- Partner with other teams to resolve cross-functional issues, including model and vehicle interface problems\n\n- Be one of the team's key hands-on developers, writing code and running experiments while setting the team's priorities\n\n\ud83e\udde9 What you\u2019ll be working on\n\n- The end-to-end driving model that powers Wayve's Robotaxi product as it launches around the world\n\n- Scaling driving performance across cities and vehicle platforms while hitting performance and compliance KPIs\n\n- Data-led iteration: using on-road and off-road evaluation to find the biggest performance gaps and close them\n\n- Working with specialists across the business to resolve model and vehicle interface issues\n\n- Growing and shaping a small, high-impact team as the Robotaxi programme scales\n\n\ud83d\ude4c You should apply if\n\nEssential\n\n- You've managed engineers before and want to lead a team while staying deeply technical. This is a Tech Lead Manager role, not a pure management role\n\n- You're highly technical and hands-on: comfortable writing Python and doing m",
